(* Wolfram Notebook File *)
(* http://www.wolfram.com/nb *)

Notebook[{
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Longitudinal p^+ integration of the NLO gluon-production term", "Title"],
Cell["Evaluate the notebook top to bottom (Evaluation > Evaluate Notebook).

We integrate

  d^3 N_NLO / d^3 k = -(1/(2 Pi)^3) (I g^4 f^{c'd'a} / (4 Pi^4)) (1/k^+)
      Int_Lam^{Vee-k^+} dp^+/(2 Pi)  Int_{w,y',z,y,x,x'}
      E^(-I k.(y'-w)) E^(-I k.(p^+/k^+)(y'-z))
      (y'-z)^m (x'-y')^k' (y-w)^i (x-z)^j
        / [ (y'-z)^2 (x'-y')^2 (y-w)^2 (x-z)^2 ]
      [ d_{k'm} d_{ij}/(p^+ + k^+) - d_{jm} d_{ik'}/p^+ - d_{im} d_{jk'}/k^+ ]
      [ color 1 ] [ color 2 ]

over p^+, in the window Vee >> k^+ >> Lam > 0.

The only p^+ dependence is the phase and the three poles.  So the p^+ integral factorizes completely out of the transverse integrals AND out of the color operators -- the Wilson lines and charges pass through untouched.  Sections 1-3 do that integral; sections 4-6 put the result back together.", "Text"]
}, Open]],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["0.  Notation", "Section"],
Cell["ASCII stand-ins for the symbols in the expression:

  kp    = k^+          omega = k.(y'-z)   (transverse dot product)
  lam   = Lambda       b     = omega/kp   (the phase is E^(-I b p^+))
  vee   = \\[Vee]        g     = coupling

Ordering assumed throughout: vee > kp > lam > 0.", "Text"],
Cell["NLOAssumptions[kp_, lam_, vee_] :=
  {kp > 0, lam > 0, vee > kp + lam, Element[{kp, lam, vee}, Reals]};", "Input"]
}, Open]],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["1.  The p^+ integral, by brute force", "Section"],
Cell["Pull the p^+-dependent factors out.  Each delta structure comes with one pole, so there are exactly three integrals to do.", "Text"],
Cell["rawIntegrals =
  Integrate[
    Exp[-I b p] {1/(p + kp), 1/p, 1/kp},
    {p, lam, vee - kp},
    Assumptions -> Append[NLOAssumptions[kp, lam, vee], b > 0]
  ]", "Input"],
Cell["i.e., with b = omega/kp,

  Int dp^+ E^(-I b p^+)/(p^+ + k^+) = E^(I b k^+) [ Ei(-I b Vee) - Ei(-I b (k^+ + Lam)) ]
  Int dp^+ E^(-I b p^+)/p^+         = Ei(-I b (Vee - k^+)) - Ei(-I b Lam)
  Int dp^+ E^(-I b p^+)/k^+         = [ E^(-I b Lam) - E^(-I b (Vee-k^+)) ] / (I b k^+)

ExpIntegralEi is evaluated just off the imaginary axis, so no branch cut is crossed for either sign of omega; the -I0 that puts it there is the usual p^+ -> p^+ - I0 prescription.", "Text"]
}, Open]],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["2.  Closed form", "Section"],
Cell["PPlusKernel returns {I1, I2, I3}, each already carrying the 1/(2 Pi) of the measure.  They multiply d_{k'm} d_{ij}, -d_{jm} d_{ik'} and -d_{im} d_{jk'} respectively.  omega = 0 is handled separately (section 3).", "Text"],
Cell["PPlusKernelCollinear[kp_, lam_, vee_] :=
  (1/(2 Pi)) {Log[vee/(kp + lam)], Log[(vee - kp)/lam], (vee - kp - lam)/kp};

PPlusKernel[omega_, kp_, lam_, vee_] :=
  If[TrueQ[PossibleZeroQ[omega]],
    PPlusKernelCollinear[kp, lam, vee],
    With[{b = omega/kp},
      (1/(2 Pi)) {
        Exp[I b kp] (ExpIntegralEi[-I b vee] - ExpIntegralEi[-I b (kp + lam)]),
        ExpIntegralEi[-I b (vee - kp)] - ExpIntegralEi[-I b lam],
        (Exp[-I b lam] - Exp[-I b (vee - kp)])/(I b kp)
      }
    ]
  ];", "Input"],
Cell["Check it against what Integrate just produced:", "Text"],
Cell["Simplify[2 Pi PPlusKernel[b kp, kp, lam, vee] - rawIntegrals,
  Assumptions -> Append[NLOAssumptions[kp, lam, vee], b > 0]]", "Input"]
}, Open]],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["3.  The regime Vee >> k^+ >> Lam", "Section"],
Cell["Two facts drive the limits:

  Ei(-I x) = EulerGamma + Log[x] - I Pi/2 + O(x)      (small x)
  Ei(-I X) -> -I Pi Sign[X]                           (|X| -> Infinity)

Valid for |omega| lam/kp << 1 << |omega| vee/kp.", "Text"],
Cell["PPlusKernelAsymptotic[omega_, kp_, lam_, vee_] :=
  With[{s = Sign[omega]},
    (1/(2 Pi)) {
      -Exp[I omega] (ExpIntegralEi[-I omega] + I Pi s),
      -EulerGamma - Log[Abs[omega] lam/kp] - I Pi s/2,
      (1 - Exp[-I omega (vee - kp)/kp])/(I omega)
    }
  ];

RapidityLog[omega_, kp_, lam_, vee_] :=
  If[TrueQ[PossibleZeroQ[omega]],
    Log[(vee - kp)/lam],
    Log[kp/(Abs[omega] lam)] - EulerGamma - I Pi Sign[omega]/2
  ];", "Input"],
Cell["2 Pi PPlusKernelAsymptotic[omega, kp, lam, vee]", "Input"],
Cell["Three things to take away, all checked numerically in section 7.

(1) Vee has dropped out of I1 and I2.  The phase, not the upper cutoff, is what regulates them once |omega| Vee/k^+ >> 1.  The one surviving cutoff dependence is the single rapidity logarithm Log[k^+/(|omega| Lam)] in I2 -- so it rides entirely on the -d_{jm} d_{ik'} structure.  That is the piece a JIMWLK-type rapidity evolution has to absorb.

(2) I3 has no pointwise Vee -> Infinity limit: its boundary term keeps oscillating with unit modulus.  It averages to zero only against a smooth transverse profile, so keep I3 exact rather than taking a limit under the y', z integrals.

(3) Do not switch the phase off in I3.  At omega -> 0 the Vee logarithm returns in I1 and I2 and I3 -> (Vee - k^+ - Lam)/k^+ diverges LINEARLY -- that term is finite only by virtue of the phase.", "Text"],
Cell["2 Pi PPlusKernelCollinear[kp, lam, vee]", "Input"],
Cell["RapidityLog[omega, kp, lam, vee]", "Input"]
}, Open]],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["4.  Transverse structure", "Section"],
Cell["Contracting the three delta structures with the numerator
  (y'-z)^m (x'-y')^k' (y-w)^i (x-z)^j
collapses it to three scalar pairings:

  d_{k'm} d_{ij} -> [(y'-z).(x'-y')] [(y-w).(x-z)]      (N1)
  d_{jm} d_{ik'} -> [(y'-z).(x-z)]   [(y-w).(x'-y')]    (N2)
  d_{im} d_{jk'} -> [(y'-z).(y-w)]   [(x-z).(x'-y')]    (N3)

Points may be given as explicit 2-component vectors (then dot products are evaluated) or as opaque symbols (then they stay inert as TDot / TSub).", "Text"],
Cell["SetAttributes[TDot, Orderless];
TDot[u_List, v_List] := u . v;
dot[u_, v_] := If[ListQ[u] && ListQ[v], u . v, TDot[u, v]];
sq[u_] := dot[u, u];
sub[u_List, v_List] := u - v;
sub[u_, v_] := TSub[u, v];

TransverseData[k_, w_, yp_, z_, y_, x_, xp_] :=
  Module[{ypz, xpyp, yw, xz},
    ypz = sub[yp, z]; xpyp = sub[xp, yp]; yw = sub[y, w]; xz = sub[x, z];
    <|
      \"ypz\" -> ypz, \"xpyp\" -> xpyp, \"yw\" -> yw, \"xz\" -> xz,
      \"N1\" -> dot[ypz, xpyp] dot[yw, xz],
      \"N2\" -> dot[ypz, xz] dot[yw, xpyp],
      \"N3\" -> dot[ypz, yw] dot[xz, xpyp],
      \"Denominator\" -> sq[ypz] sq[xpyp] sq[yw] sq[xz],
      \"Phase\" -> Exp[-I dot[k, sub[yp, w]]],
      \"omega\" -> dot[k, ypz]
    |>
  ];

TransverseFactor[d_Association, {i1_, i2_, i3_}] :=
  d[\"Phase\"] (d[\"N1\"] i1 - d[\"N2\"] i2 - d[\"N3\"] i3) / d[\"Denominator\"];", "Input"],
Cell["TableForm[
  Transpose[{{\"d_{k'm} d_{ij}\", \"d_{jm} d_{ik'}\", \"d_{im} d_{jk'}\"},
    Lookup[TransverseData[k, w, yp, z, y, x, xp], {\"N1\", \"N2\", \"N3\"}]}],
  TableHeadings -> {None, {\"delta structure\", \"transverse contraction\"}}]", "Input"]
}, Open]],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["5.  Color structure", "Section"],
Cell["Untouched by the p^+ integration -- kept inert.  U[a,b][pt] is the adjoint Wilson line U^{ab}(pt), Rho[a][pt] the color charge rho^a(pt), FStruct the structure constant.  Repeated adjoint indices are summed.", "Text"],
Cell["ColorStructure[idx_Association] :=
  Module[{a, b, c, d, e, cp, dp, ep, w, yp, z, y, x, xp},
    {a, b, c, d, e} = Lookup[idx, {\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\", \"e\"}];
    {cp, dp, ep} = Lookup[idx, {\"cp\", \"dp\", \"ep\"}];
    {w, yp, z, y, x, xp} = Lookup[idx, {\"w\", \"yp\", \"z\", \"y\", \"x\", \"xp\"}];
    FStruct[cp, dp, a] *
      NonCommutativeMultiply[
        (U[ep, cp][yp] ** U[dp, b][z] ** Rho[ep][xp]
           - U[b, dp][z] ** U[cp, ep][xp] ** Rho[ep][xp]),
        (U[b, c][z] ** U[a, d][y] ** U[c, e][x] ** Rho[d][y] ** Rho[e][x]
           - U[a, d][y] ** Rho[d][y] ** Rho[b][x])
      ]
  ];", "Input"]
}, Open]],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["6.  Assembly", "Section"],
Cell["The full integrand with the p^+ integration done, transverse integrals left inert.  Option \"Kernel\" selects \"Exact\" (default), \"Asymptotic\" or \"Collinear\".

Note on the measure: as written it is Int_{w,y',z,y,x}, but the integrand contains x' (in (x'-y') and rho^{e'}(x')).  NLOResult integrates over {w, y', z, y, x, x'}; if x' is meant to be tied to another point, substitute for it first.", "Text"],
Cell["Options[NLOIntegrand] = {\"Kernel\" -> \"Exact\"};

NLOIntegrand[k_, w_, yp_, z_, y_, x_, xp_, kp_, lam_, vee_, g_,
    idx_Association, OptionsPattern[]] :=
  Module[{data, omega, kern, pref},
    data = TransverseData[k, w, yp, z, y, x, xp];
    omega = data[\"omega\"];
    kern = Switch[OptionValue[\"Kernel\"],
      \"Exact\", PPlusKernel[omega, kp, lam, vee],
      \"Asymptotic\", PPlusKernelAsymptotic[omega, kp, lam, vee],
      \"Collinear\", PPlusKernelCollinear[kp, lam, vee]];
    pref = -(1/(2 Pi)^3) (I g^4/(4 Pi^4)) (1/kp);
    pref TransverseFactor[data, kern] ColorStructure[idx]
  ];

NLOResult[k_, w_, yp_, z_, y_, x_, xp_, kp_, lam_, vee_, g_,
    idx_Association, opts : OptionsPattern[NLOIntegrand]] :=
  Inactive[Integrate][
    NLOIntegrand[k, w, yp, z, y, x, xp, kp, lam, vee, g, idx, opts],
    {w, yp, z, y, x, xp}
  ];", "Input"],
Cell["idx = <|\"a\" -> a, \"b\" -> b, \"c\" -> c, \"d\" -> d, \"e\" -> e,
        \"cp\" -> cp, \"dp\" -> dp, \"ep\" -> ep,
        \"w\" -> w, \"yp\" -> yp, \"z\" -> z, \"y\" -> y, \"x\" -> x, \"xp\" -> xp|>;
NLOResult[k, w, yp, z, y, x, xp, kp, lam, vee, g, idx]", "Input"]
}, Open]],
Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["7.  Numerical audit", "Section"],
Cell["Exact kernel vs direct NIntegrate over p^+, and the asymptotic kernel vs the exact one (I1, I2 only -- I3 keeps its boundary oscillation).  Expect ~1*^-16 for the first and ~1*^-9, i.e. O(Lam, k^+/(omega Vee)), for the second.", "Text"],
Cell["cases = {{0.37, 1.0, 0.013, 260.0}, {-0.37, 1.0, 0.013, 260.0},
         {2.5, 1.0, 0.013, 260.0}, {-1.1, 3.0, 0.05, 900.0},
         {0.9, 2.0, 0.002, 5000.0}};

numKernel[{om_, kp_, lam_, vee_}] :=
  (1/(2 Pi)) NIntegrate[Exp[-I p om/kp] {1/(p + kp), 1/p, 1/kp},
    {p, lam, vee - kp}, Method -> \"LevinRule\", MaxRecursion -> 60,
    AccuracyGoal -> 12, PrecisionGoal -> 10];

<|
  \"ExactVsNIntegrate\" ->
    Max[Abs[Flatten[(PPlusKernel @@@ cases) - (numKernel /@ cases)]]],
  \"AsymptoticVsExact\" ->
    Max[Abs[Flatten[(PPlusKernelAsymptotic[#[[1]], #[[2]], 10^-8, 10^9] -
        PPlusKernel[#[[1]], #[[2]], 10^-8, 10^9])[[{1, 2}]] & /@ cases]]]
|>", "Input"],
Cell["And the reassembled transverse factor against a direct one-dimensional integration of the whole bracket, at an arbitrary configuration of points:", "Text"],
Cell["{kv, wv, ypv, zv, yv, xv, xpv} =
  {{0.8, -0.5}, {0.1, 0.2}, {1.3, -0.4}, {-0.6, 0.9},
   {0.35, 1.1}, {-1.2, -0.7}, {0.9, 0.15}};
{kp0, lam0, vee0} = {1.0, 0.01, 400.0};
dat = TransverseData[kv, wv, ypv, zv, yv, xv, xpv];

assembled = TransverseFactor[dat, PPlusKernel[dat[\"omega\"], kp0, lam0, vee0]];

direct = Exp[-I kv . (ypv - wv)]/
    (((ypv - zv) . (ypv - zv)) ((xpv - ypv) . (xpv - ypv))
      ((yv - wv) . (yv - wv)) ((xv - zv) . (xv - zv))) *
  NIntegrate[
    Exp[-I p (kv . (ypv - zv))/kp0]/(2 Pi) (
      ((ypv - zv) . (xpv - ypv)) ((yv - wv) . (xv - zv))/(p + kp0)
      - ((ypv - zv) . (xv - zv)) ((yv - wv) . (xpv - ypv))/p
      - ((ypv - zv) . (yv - wv)) ((xv - zv) . (xpv - ypv))/kp0),
    {p, lam0, vee0 - kp0}, Method -> \"LevinRule\", MaxRecursion -> 60,
    AccuracyGoal -> 12];

<|\"omega\" -> dat[\"omega\"], \"assembled\" -> assembled, \"direct\" -> direct,
  \"difference\" -> Abs[assembled - direct]|>", "Input"]
}, Open]]
},
WindowSize->{1100, 850},
WindowMargins->Automatic,
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb"
]
